                                "sense_id": "e1e8fbf5-5a09-375b-ad97-0b735b65e6ad",
                                "text": "But [Assistant to the Solicitor General Austin] Raynor relied on this distinction – whether proceedings are pending, or all proceedings have ended – to argue that the court’s 2001 decision interpreting the post-removal order statute, Zadvydas v. Davis, was inapposite."
                            }
                        ]
